    "**Reviewed (30 October):** the hero chip says Past target, the app's own word for waits past their target, because the ED strip uses overdue for typed form times. The ED strip names its noun (1 form due, No forms due) and an ED with nobody waiting just says No wait. The checks chip reads 2 to check, and the desktop hero says in transit, as the phone does.",
    "**Consistent controls (30 October):** every tab row is one size (a 40px track with 30px tabs at 13px; 32px tabs on a phone with a 48px tap area), every Show more is the same centred row, every text link is 13px, and names in Planned and Activity match Waiting's.",
    "**Placement redesigned (30 October), from a copy of today's panel so every action, guard and record works as now:** the wards that fit lead, with fits with no bed now under them; the 14 wards that need an override reason and the wards that cannot take the person sit behind one disclosure each, with their counts. Each ward is two lines (name and road time, then its beds). The phone uses the desktop's two fact lines instead of the four-box grid, and the tier sits beside the name.",
    '**Placement checks:** the header\'s "Checks: 9 of 9 met" and its filter are gone. They described the first ward on the list without naming it, so they read as facts about the patient; the checks now sit once, as "Checks for BTY Adult Secure", with "9 of 9 met". With a ward chosen, Refer leads on its own row and Quick send and Override share the row under it.',
    "**Changed on purpose:** today's panel never collapses wards a coordinator can act on. Here the override-only wards are behind a disclosure that states the count and opens itself while one of them is chosen. For Josh to confirm before this goes into the app.",
